        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; late-event determination remains incomplete\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Required item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | Sep-25 — `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable in the authorized records |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Indeterminate** |\n\nThe Pending Close timestamp is reproduced exactly; the source provides no timezone or UTC offset.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe supplied, authorized `state.db` extract contains work-order and cost-period records but **no cost-event rows**. Supporting records—and their cache copies—are restricted to the records-custodian role. I requested an authorized disclosure, but none was available. Consequently, I cannot establish either that a late event exists or that no late event occurred.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle’s supplied 26B documentation states that newly created transactions relating to the Pending Close period or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nThus, processing a newly created, non-exempt September transaction while the period remained Pending Close would be inconsistent with that treatment. Assessing this particular event requires its type, creation timestamp, and recorded accounting status.\n\n*Sources: supplied `state.db` extract, `work_orders` and `cost_periods`; Oracle 26B documentation, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.*\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial report and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_f5b9f3583275/audit-report.json` and submitted with review state **`needs_evidence`**.",
